Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Test output
coverage/
test/**/failures/

# App artifacts
*.rackpal.bak
*.rackpal.autosave

# Release staging (tools/release/make_portable.ps1)
dist/

# SIGNING KEY MATERIAL -- NEVER COMMIT ANY OF THIS.
# DR-006 self-signs, which makes the private key cheap to re-mint and
# therefore tempting to check in "just for the build agent". Do not. A
# committed key is a key every clone can sign as, and a self-signed
# publisher the org has told its machines to TRUST (LocalMachine\
# TrustedPublisher) is exactly the certificate you least want loose.
# The public .cer is the half that gets distributed, and it is deployed by
# GPO rather than from this repository.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
*.key

# Python (tools/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# REAL CLIENT DRAWINGS ARE NEVER COMMITTED, AND GIT IS WHY
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# `docs/reference/` holds product photographs and manufacturer technical
# drawings, which are tracked. A real job's plan set is a different thing
# and is not: it carries a licensed engineer's seal and licence number,
# the firm's name, the builder's mark and a client's address, and a
# redaction that covers the address does not cover any of the rest.
#
# THE REASON IS THAT GIT HISTORY IS PERMANENT AND DR-036 IS PENDING. A
# public GPLv3 release publishes every commit ever made, not the current
# tree, so a plan set committed today and deleted tomorrow ships anyway.
# Nothing in this product needs one in the repository: the measurements
# taken from a plan set are recorded in docs/12 with the method beside
# them, so anybody can re-run them against their own sheet (docs/12
# section 5.9.5).
#
# The pattern is deliberately TOP-LEVEL ONLY: a single `*` does not cross
# a `/`, so `keystone/technical drawings/*.pdf` stays tracked without
# needing a negation to rescue it. Broadening this to `**` would silently
# untrack seven manufacturer drawings the catalogue cites.
docs/reference/*.pdf
